{
 "id": "fox-vs-crouch-cancel",
 "name": "Beat crouch cancel",
 "part": "neutral",
 "characters": [
  "fox"
 ],
 "goal": "Against a crouching opponent, grab or down air into shine instead of the neutral air",
 "why": "A crouching opponent takes a weak hit with almost no stun and stays on the ground: after Fox's neutral air it acts before he does and hits him as he lands. A grab ignores the crouch, and the down air's hits keep it in stun until Fox has landed and shined.",
 "switch": "success",
 "reset": {
  "after": "quiet",
  "seconds": 1
 },
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "The opponent moves about and crouches when Fox comes close. Grab it with Z, or short hop a down air onto it and shine as he lands.",
  "expect": "Each try begins with Fox's jump, grab or shine next to it and is judged when he has it grabbed, when his shine hits, or when it hits him: hit after any opener, the try is lost.",
  "example": [
   {
    "stick": [
     0.3,
     0
    ],
    "frame": 1,
    "hold": 900
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     0,
     0
    ],
    "frame": 1,
    "hold": 900,
    "from": {
     "near": 10.0
    }
   },
   {
    "press": "Z",
    "frame": 13,
    "hold": 1,
    "from": {
     "near": 10.0
    }
   }
  ],
  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: Z. The grab",
   "7": "Frame {f}: it has {opp}"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "What the crouch does",
    "text": [
     "{opp} is crouching at 0%. Fox's neutral air hits it and barely moves it: it can act again before Fox has landed and his landing lag is over.",
     "Its {answer} is already out when he can act. Against a crouch at low damage the neutral air loses."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         0.3,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 900
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 900,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 13,
        "hold": 1,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "A",
        "frame": "J+1+12",
        "hold": 1,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "L",
        "frame": 37,
        "hold": 2,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: a short hop",
       "J+1": "Frame {J+1}: A. The neutral air hits, and {opp} stays down",
       "25": "Frame {f}: L before the landing"
      },
      "cues": [
       {
        "frames": [
         "J+1",
         24
        ],
        "words": "The neutral air: it barely flinches",
        "kind": "info"
       },
       {
        "frames": [
         25,
         60
        ],
        "words": "It acts first: its {answer}",
        "kind": "late"
       }
      ]
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "The grab",
    "text": [
     "A grab does not care whether its target stands or crouches. Z next to it, or out of a dash: X or Y and then Z, the jump-cancelled grab.",
     "From the grab, the up throw starts Fox's combos."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         0.3,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 900
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 900,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       },
       {
        "press": "Z",
        "frame": 13,
        "hold": 1,
        "from": {
         "near": 10.0
        }
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: Z. The grab",
       "7": "Frame {f}: it has {opp}"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  ]
 },
